# Line endings are LF everywhere, including in a Windows working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default, and set on at least one
# machine here — hands the working tree CRLF while Prettier is configured for LF. The
# result is that `pnpm format:check` fails locally on 55 files nobody has edited, and
# passes in CI on Linux. A verification step that disagrees with CI is worse than none:
# it trains you to ignore it, and then it stops catching the real failures too.
#
# `eol=lf` makes checkout produce LF regardless of the local autocrlf setting, so the
# working tree, the repository and CI all agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched by any of the above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
